Clinical Interventions: Initiated aggressive oral rehydration therapy with high-sodium electrolyte solutions. Strictly mandated the immediate resumption of Pancreatic Enzyme Replacement Therapy (PERT) with all meals and snacks.
Positive Behavioral Change: To eliminate the severe stomach cramps and regain your energy, you must commit to taking your digestive enzymes with the very first bite of every meal. Set an alert on your phone for lunch and dinner times. When you take the capsules and subsequently experience a meal without the severe bloating and cramps, internally acknowledge that you actively controlled your symptoms. This absence of pain will serve as the powerful reward for sticking to your enzyme routine.
Home-Based Services (Optional): None.
DME/Safety (Optional): None.
Follow-up: Urgent referral to the regional Cystic Fibrosis multidisciplinary clinic tomorrow morning for comprehensive nutritional and respiratory optimization.

SAFETY-NETTING ESCALATION PLAN

Proceed immediately to the Emergency Department if the abdominal pain becomes sharp, constant, and unbearable, if you begin vomiting green fluid, or if you feel completely unable to stand without fainting.

